A grid is a layout that has rows and columns.
Set a display property to grid i.e display: grid; then set number of columns grid must have e.g (grid-template-columns: 100px 100px 200px;) where the columns will have width in regards to the selected quantity(100px).
When a div is placed inside a grid it only takes the entire column instead of the entire line even though they are block elements by default.
The number of values passed in gride-template-column determines the number of columns and the value itself determines the width of the column.
Whenever we have more elements than we have columns, it will wrap around and create new rows.
fr is a special value in GRID that stands for free space meaning it takes up the amount of space remaining on the grid.
1fr tells the columns to take the remaining amount of space and the number in front of it telss us relatively how much of the remaining space this column gets.